    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\$362.43$ per quarter.",
      "worked": "The quarterly rate is $10\\%\\div4=2.5\\%$, and there are $3\\times4=12$ payments. The future value of $\\$1$ table gives $13.7956$ for 12 periods at 2.5% per period.\n\nLet $M$ be the deposit at the end of each quarter.\n$$\\begin{align*}FV&=\\text{FV of }\\$1\\times M\\\\5000&=13.7956M\\\\M&=\\frac{5000}{13.7956}\\\\M&\\approx\\$362.43\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
